From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:35:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] [GLM5Next] Compute the indexer head gate from BF16 with
 FP32 output

The kpool indexer computes its head-gate weights in FP32, because BF16
rounding can flip near-tie pool rankings at long context. It did so by
upcasting the hidden states every call and running an FP32 GEMM against
an FP32 copy of the weight; on GB10 cuBLAS's FP32 small-N kernel took
~69 us per layer.

Run the GEMM on the BF16 operands with FP32 accumulation and FP32
output (torch.mm(..., out_dtype=torch.float32)). The output stays FP32
as before. BF16 x BF16 products are exact in FP32, so the result matches
the FP32 GEMM up to summation order; it is not bit-identical. The cached
weight is now a view of the loaded BF16 weight instead of an FP32 copy,
which also saves that copy's memory.

Source: kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 @ c748079,
  experimental/fixes/attention.py (base vLLM ddd6fbca), by Matt
  Mastracci; porting authorized by the owner. knapcio's
  overlay/glm_small_gemv.py (GLM_GATE_GEMV, MIT) targets the same GEMM
  (66.8 us) with a Triton split-K kernel and was not used.
Upstream: absent in v0.31.0 and main.
Claimed gain: Kindling (4x GB10, TP=4): removes ~69 us per indexer
  layer per step (11 layers). knapcio (4x GB10, TP=4): its gate GEMV
  is part of -1.25 ms per c1 decode step together with two other
  changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vllm/models/glm5next/common/attention.py | 17 ++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/attention.py b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/attention.py
index f39c3a7cd..99e783f85 100644
--- a/vllm/models/glm5next/common/attention.py
+++ b/vllm/models/glm5next/common/attention.py
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@ class Indexer(nn.Module):
         self.scale_fmt = "ue8m0"
         self.quant_block_size = 128  # TODO: get from config
         self.topk_indices_buffer = topk_indices_buffer
-        self._wp_fp32: torch.Tensor | None = None
+        self._wp_t: torch.Tensor | None = None
 
         # NOTE: (zyongye) we use fp8 naive cache,
         #       where we store value in fp8 and scale in fp32
@@ -337,14 +337,13 @@ class Indexer(nn.Module):
         # rankings on long-context tasks. Cache it after weights are loaded.
         kw, _ = self.wk_weights_proj(hidden_states)
         k = kw[:, : self.head_dim]
-        if self._wp_fp32 is None:
-            self._wp_fp32 = (
-                self.wk_weights_proj.weight.data[self.head_dim :, :]
-                .t()
-                .contiguous()
-                .float()
-            )
-        weights = torch.mm(hidden_states.float(), self._wp_fp32)
+        # BF16 inputs with FP32 accumulation and output: the products are exact
+        # in FP32, so this matches an FP32 GEMM up to summation order, without
+        # FP32 copies of the operands (cuBLAS's FP32 small-N GEMM took ~69 us
+        # per layer on GB10).
+        if self._wp_t is None:
+            self._wp_t = self.wk_weights_proj.weight.data[self.head_dim :, :].t()
+        weights = torch.mm(hidden_states, self._wp_t, out_dtype=torch.float32)
 
         k = _fused_indexer_k_norm(
             k, self.k_norm.weight, self.k_norm.bias, self.head_dim, self.k_norm.eps
